{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Additional local gate occurrence while validating epidemic-chocolaty-imago at code revision e48142648445e6f947e46183a99097bfdbc45366. The documented macOS CI-equivalent default suite completed 16406 passed / 55 skipped but xdist killed two workers at the 300-second per-test limit while running test_code_review_gate_session.py::test_local_session_review_creates_reuses_artifact_with_session_and_deps and ::test_pass1_finder_receives_no_prior_findings. A serial reproduction of the same nodes also timed out; the thread dump proved the first node was blocked at rebar._snapshot.git_fetch.interprocess_lock -> fcntl.flock(LOCK_EX) from resolve_gate_handle/acquire/resolve_ref/fetch_origin, before the test behavior ran. After the external lock holder cleared (lsof reported no holder and no pytest/review process remained), the exact nodes passed independently in 9.69s and 5.26s. This parallel/blocked versus cleared/serialized control matches this bug’s confirmed cross-process fetch-lock mechanism. No duplicate bug or footprint-scope workaround was created."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787538896559601001,"uuid":"e1489731-5f0c-4168-aba1-643c0f9689c3"}